  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "As you can see almost all of the data types of the columns are `text`,
      even the dates! \r

      \r

      This is expected since the dataset comes from a text-based format (csv),
      there is no native metadata for pandas to infer to. In this silver layer,
      is where we cast later on these datatypes to its proper datatype.\r

      \r

      From what I can see the proper datatypes of these fields would be:\r

      - Date columns: `Date`\r

      - application_ID and salary: `INTEGER`\r

      - the rest : `TEXT`\r

      \r\n"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "## Categorical Values"
    metadata: {}
  - kind: 1
    languageId: markdown
    value: "### Casing Problem"
    metadata: {}
